# =============================================================================
# ThreadSanitizer suppression file
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=scripts/tsan.supp ctest --preset tsan
#
# The `tsan` test preset in CMakePresets.json applies this automatically.
#
# Keep this file as small as possible: every entry is a blind spot. Prefer
# fixing the race. Entries here are limited to behaviour that is deliberate and
# that TSan has no way to recognise as such.
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# abandon_thread() intentionally neither joins nor detaches.
#
# See src/utility.cpp: for a std::thread handle inherited across fork(), glibc's
# pthread_detach dereferences a thread descriptor the child's fork() already
# reclaimed and segfaults, so the agent ends the thread object's lifetime by
# reusing its storage instead. The OS thread has already run to completion; only
# the handle is dropped. TSan's thread-leak detector reports any never-joined
# thread, so it flags the test that covers this on purpose.
#
# Scoped to that one test rather than disabling report_thread_leaks globally,
# which would hide genuinely leaked worker threads everywhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
thread:AbandonThreadDoesNotAllocateAndClearsHandle
